    "report": "Verdict: NEEDS_WORK\n\nThe candidate fails on multiple acceptance criteria. Findings (line numbers refer to the captured candidate text; note the provided \"Original:\" block was empty, so comparison is against the stated acceptance criteria):\n\n1. Bool type leak (lines 27, 33): pending count — `isinstance(True, int)` is True, so `pending_reviews: True` renders as \"True\", not \"unknown\". The spec requires \"nonnegative integer\" and elsewhere explicitly excludes bool (line 34 does exclude bool for observed_at/now; pending does not).\n\n2. Line 34 age check: `isinstance(observed, (int, float)) and math.isfinite(observed)` — works, but note `math.isfinite` on a bool passes; the spec says \"exact int/float types (not bool)\". Candidate does NOT exclude bool here: `isinstance(True, (int, float))` is True and `math.isfinite(True)` is finite, so `observed_at: True` with `now: 2` would produce age \"1.0 seconds (fresh)\" instead of \"unknown\". Same for `now: True`.\n\n3. Line 47: `wait_label = 'none' if wait_reason is None or not isinstance(wait_reason, str) else wait_reason` — spec says LABEL is \"none\" when wait_reason is **absent OR None**; the candidate conflates \"absent\" with \"None\" correctly via `.get()` default (absent → None → 'none', OK), but then \"All other types/strings render unknown\" — a non-string (e.g., 5, True, list) should render \"unknown\", and the candidate does that via the `not isinstance` branch only when wait_reason is not None... actually re-reading: non-string non-None goes to else? No — `wait_reason is None or not isinstance(..., str)` → 'none'. So `wait_reason: 5` renders \"none\", not \"unknown\". That violates \"all other types render unknown, never raw input\". Bug.\n\n4. Line 57: `'LAST OBSERVED reviewer state: '` — uppercase mismatch; original line is presumably \"Last observed reviewer state: \" (the spec says preserve all existing output lines and order). Uppercase changes the existing line, failing \"preserve all existing output lines\".\n\n5. Line 17 scheduler allowed set `{'ready','held','not_started'}` and line 21 reviewer set, line 29 build-ID regex — not verifiable against original since the provided original was empty; cannot confirm these match \"existing behavior\". This makes full verification partial.\n\n6. No syntax check was run (no output proves it); I did not execute the file.\n\nPASS would require: fix pending bool exclusion, exclude bool for observed_at/now, render non-string non-None wait_reason as \"unknown\", restore the reviewer line's original casing, and confirm scheduler/reviewer/build-regex match the true baseline (original source not visible in the capture — empty under \"Original:\").",
